Subject: [PATCH 10/12] turnip: Adreno 710/720/722 GMEM tile pitch alignment and artifact fix (Vauzi-17)

Integrates Vauzi-17 community patch for Adreno 710, 720, and 722 GPUs to enforce
strict 64/128-byte stride alignment on GMEM tile load/store operations, resolving
horizontal striping, color banding, and texture shear in Switch emulators.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
index 3344556..778899a 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pass.cc
@@ -520,6 +520,20 @@ tu_setup_tiling_config(struct tu_render_pass *pass,
    if (dev->info.chip == 710 || dev->info.chip == 720 || dev->info.chip == 722) {
+      /* Vauzi-17: Align tile width and pitch to eliminate GMEM banding */
+      tiling->tile_align_w = ALIGN(tiling->tile_align_w, 64);
+      tiling->tile_align_h = ALIGN(tiling->tile_align_h, 32);
+      tiling->force_gmem_stride_clamp = true;
+   }
